# Google Drive sync. Optional — with this unset the whole sync panel hides
# itself and the app is exactly what it was before: local-only, no account, no
# network. Set it and Settings grows a "Google Drive sync" panel.
#
# The client ID is PUBLIC by design. Google's browser token flow has no client
# secret at all: the only thing that stops another site using this ID is the
# list of Authorized JavaScript origins on the OAuth client itself. So this
# value is safe in a repo, in a bundle, and in a Vercel environment variable —
# and there is nothing here to rotate or leak.
#
# TWO STEPS BEFORE IT WORKS, both in Google Cloud Console, and both only doable
# by whoever owns the OAuth client:
#
#   1. Add this app's origins to the client's Authorized JavaScript origins:
#      http://localhost:5173, http://localhost:4173, https://read.flyleaf.cc,
#      and https://flyleaf-ereader.vercel.app. Google refuses the token request
#      with `origin_mismatch` from anywhere not on that list, and this is the
#      ONE step that cannot be done from the repo. Until it is done, Connect
#      fails — but it now fails out loud, naming the origin, rather than
#      claiming the window was closed. See SPEC.md § 15.1.
#   2. Set VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in the Vercel project (all environments).
#      Done — it is set for production, preview and development. It is a
#      build-time import.meta.env value, so changing it needs a fresh deploy.
#
# The scopes the app asks for are drive.appdata — a hidden folder the reader
# never sees in their Drive — and userinfo.email, only so the panel can say
# which account it is syncing to.
#
# This is the ID Flyleaf Press already uses. Sharing it means one OAuth client
# and one consent screen for both apps, and it also means ONE hidden folder:
# `appDataFolder` is scoped to the client, not to an app, so Press's backup and
# this app's sit side by side in it. That is why every write here is tagged and
# why the delete filters on the tag (see the note on `APP` in src/sync/drive.ts)
# — without it, one app's "remove the copy from my Drive" takes the other's
# backup with it. See SPEC.md § 15.1.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=997776608568-vfq90f4v1b1v82p2enm0li1f4sj72vrk.apps.googleusercontent.com
